    "boundary": "Minimal unit/stat structs and direct percentage helper. ExecuteEvents is a stub; ExecuteMissileDamage only captures packets. Does not certify source mitigation, event ordering, PvP final reduction or modern internals. Result flags0x4021 include SOFTHIT0x4000. Probe wrapper now includes the unmodified two-line ExecuteEvents physical/life clip before flat and percentage calls; it does not reproduce the full routine.",
    "originalEventTailFragment": "const int32_t nHp = STATLIST_UnitGetStatValue(pDefender, STAT_HITPOINTS, 0); pDamage->dwPhysDamage = std::min(pDamage->dwPhysDamage, nHp);"
  },
  "mechanics": "Free selected-right aura, first/periodic50-frame pulses, existing51-frame recipient leases. Flat stat stored as lease.Percent, percentage as lease.DamagePercent; values use effective rank. Flat physical damage on eligible melee attempt, including miss/zero/blocked consumer paths. Distinct percentage packet uses prepared physical FP256 after mitigation and capped to remaining defender FP256 life before the incoming hit is applied. Nonweapon/ranged packets do not retaliate. Returned damage is not another melee/weapon hit: no recursive Thorns, leech, ordinary strike procs or outgoing Might enhancement. Returned packet receives attacker Energy Shield/Bone Armor/physical resistance/flat reduction. Fractional return debt retained. Legacy player/hireling percent is (percent+4)/8; native BaseHire classification is a provisional shared-world projection.",
  "nativePatch": {
    "path": "patches/ModernUO/0057-melee-attempt-and-prepared-physical-damage.patch",
    "scope": "Optional content hooks only; no Server-engine edit. ClassSkillDamage retains original2-argument constructor and adds optional init-only Physical256. BaseWeapon hit/miss scopes; AOS prepared callback before damage including early zero-total case. Root bridges player basic/Poison Dagger, class summons/monsters, typed/Gear/elite weapon paths.",
    "counts": {
      "ModernUO": 57,
      "ClassicUO": 36
    },
    "replay": "All touched sources reverse/replay byte-equal in disposable copies."
  },
